{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1311149-do-you-allow-your-players-to-transform-instantly-into-crinos","id":1311149,"title":"Do you allow your players to transform instantly into Crinos?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-05-09T21:54:55-07:00","id":1311149,"title":"Do you allow your players to transform instantly into Crinos?","content":"Or do you make them spend Rage to do so, or only a primal-urge roll is enough?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T22:32:07-07:00","id":1311159,"title":"","content":"There's nothing special about Crinos here. What it takes is variable. Metis can do it reflexively, certain Merits and Gifts can influence it, non-Metis can always spend a Rage for it, or you can roll for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T22:34:36-07:00","id":1311160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1311149-do-you-allow-your-players-to-transform-instantly-into-crinos?p=1311159#post1311159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's nothing special about Crinos here. What it takes is variable. Metis can do it reflexively, certain Merits and Gifts can influence it, non-Metis can always spend a Rage for it, or you can roll for it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But what do YOU think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T23:20:57-07:00","id":1311168,"title":"","content":"I think the rules are fine as-is and there's no compelling reason to muck with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T23:34:35-07:00","id":1311169,"title":"","content":"I see, but if I'm not mistaken using a primal urge roll you have to go through the forms and not straight to the form you want, isn't it right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T23:57:47-07:00","id":1311170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1311149-do-you-allow-your-players-to-transform-instantly-into-crinos?p=1311169#post1311169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see, but if I'm not mistaken using a primal urge roll you have to go through the forms and not straight to the form you want, isn't it right?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Unless they are metis, or have a merit or a gift.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-10T00:09:57-07:00","id":1311171,"title":"","content":"I see, so I remember right. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-10T01:26:56-07:00","id":1311177,"title":"","content":"Well, go through a form. Since Crinos is in the middle, you never need to go through more than one intermediary form (Homid to Glabro to Crinos, or Lupus to Hispo to Crinos). So it's a Stamina + Primal Urge extended roll (that is you can keep rolling multiple turns in a row as long as you don't botch) at diff 6 that requires 2 success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-10T01:29:08-07:00","id":1311179,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but in combat in WoD, 1 turn makes ALL the difference!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-10T02:00:38-07:00","id":1311182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1311149-do-you-allow-your-players-to-transform-instantly-into-crinos?p=1311179#post1311179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but in combat in WoD, 1 turn makes ALL the difference!</div> </div> </div> </div>Not as much as preparation. Going into a combat where one turn changing matters.... is already sub optimal. OF course Hispo is also a pretty awesome killing form too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-10T02:02:23-07:00","id":1311184,"title":"","content":"Surely, I just said that because it matters and specifically in the case I'm thinkng in game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-10T10:22:13-07:00","id":1311243,"title":"","content":"Right... if werewolves have time, even 10 seconds, to get ready, they're going to be in the form they want to be in. If they have zero time to prepare, they have to choose between taking a turn (or potentially more if the dice hate them) or spending a bit of Rage... or just have a 7 pt Merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-10T13:29:22-07:00","id":1311279,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12348_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12348\" data-vbnamecard=\"12348\">Herr Meister</a> I allow it if a character gets 5 successes on the shifting roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-10T14:23:22-07:00","id":1311285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1311149-do-you-allow-your-players-to-transform-instantly-into-crinos?p=1311243#post1311243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right... if werewolves have time, even 10 seconds, to get ready, they're going to be in the form they want to be in. If they have zero time to prepare, they have to choose between taking a turn (or potentially more if the dice hate them) or spending a bit of Rage... or just have a 7 pt Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Isn't &quot;Entering combat&quot; a way to get rage... or is that just a house rule we've been playing with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-10T14:57:21-07:00","id":1311291,"title":"","content":"Somewhere between.<br /> <br /> The start of a tense situation can get you Rage as emotions start to rile up; including a fight about to start. But it's going to be situational, not automatic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-10T23:34:50-07:00","id":1311348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1311149-do-you-allow-your-players-to-transform-instantly-into-crinos?p=1311285#post1311285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Isn't &quot;Entering combat&quot; a way to get rage... or is that just a house rule we've been playing with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Entering any kind of strong emotion actually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T03:36:12-07:00","id":1311372,"title":"","content":"Rage or Primal Urge roll, also nothing stopping someone who chooses to roll also spending for Rage actions (although it's more efficient to rage to Crinos)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-12T19:28:05-07:00","id":1311687,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, other WoD games tend to assume that it doesn't take much time for werewolves to change, perhaps assuming that Rage would always end up spent. In fact, Avenger Imbued even began to refer to Garou as &quot;flickers&quot; because of this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T02:03:25-07:00","id":1311730,"title":"","content":"If you need to get into actions instantly, spend Rage. That\u2019s what it\u2019s for. If you have time, take it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T20:39:19-07:00","id":1311968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1311149-do-you-allow-your-players-to-transform-instantly-into-crinos?p=1311730#post1311730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you need to get into actions instantly, spend Rage. That\u2019s what it\u2019s for. If you have time, take it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not if you want to use Gnosis - like for Spirit of the Fray","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T22:58:47-07:00","id":1311990,"title":"","content":"Spending Gnosis on SotF is only really worth it if you're up against other things with super Init, or if you're using optional/house rules on Init. Most of the time the Gnosis on it isn't worth it for one turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-14T00:25:20-07:00","id":1312005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1311149-do-you-allow-your-players-to-transform-instantly-into-crinos?p=1311968#post1311968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not if you want to use Gnosis - like for Spirit of the Fray</div> </div> </div> </div>If you\u2019re caught flat footed and need to choose one or the other, well done for your attacker. They\u2019ve managed to get an advantage. Maybe your Garou should be better prepared next time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-14T00:42:21-07:00","id":1312011,"title":"","content":"There's other options that I remember, even if I'm rusty on Werewolf; spending a gnosis to come through and attack from the Umbra, Jam tech in the opening round to deal with firearms, Spiritual wrath so they can't soak an attack, and not to mention activating Luna's Armour","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-14T02:20:15-07:00","id":1312020,"title":"","content":"Yes, if we cherry pick the perfect selection of Gnosis based combat Gifts, it might be worth it to spend Gnosis on SotF and go first to use those instead of spending Rage on shifting. At least until you throw Chaos Mechanics into the mix and can do both.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile in normal play, SotF puts a combat focused Garou so high up the initiative roster every round with it's passive bonus, that they're going to act before 99.9% of things in the WoD that don't also have SotF, so they're not going to worry about the Gnosis option the vast majority of the time.<br /> <br /> Gnosis also isn't as free flowing as Rage or WP, so tossing 5 Gnosis out on the first round of combat is... probably not a great idea.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T15:01:17-07:00","id":1312420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1311149-do-you-allow-your-players-to-transform-instantly-into-crinos?p=1312005#post1312005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you\u2019re caught flat footed and need to choose one or the other, well done for your attacker. They\u2019ve managed to get an advantage. Maybe your Garou should be better prepared next time.</div> </div> </div> </div>That really only applies to monstrously fast enemies. After all, even without Gnosis expenditure, SotF adds a flat +10 to your initiative that will likely put you at the top of the list whatever you roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T16:30:22-07:00","id":1312439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1311149-do-you-allow-your-players-to-transform-instantly-into-crinos?p=1312020#post1312020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, if we cherry pick the perfect selection of Gnosis based combat Gifts, it might be worth it to spend Gnosis on SotF and go first to use those instead of spending Rage on shifting. At least until you throw Chaos Mechanics into the mix and can do both.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile in normal play, SotF puts a combat focused Garou so high up the initiative roster every round with it's passive bonus, that they're going to act before 99.9% of things in the WoD that don't also have SotF, so they're not going to worry about the Gnosis option the vast majority of the time.<br /> <br /> Gnosis also isn't as free flowing as Rage or WP, so tossing 5 Gnosis out on the first round of combat is... probably not a great idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't talking about using ALL of them at once, but for the situations that any one of those gifts would be a powerful opening move","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T16:55:02-07:00","id":1312443,"title":"","content":"The problem is most of the Gnosis based combat Gifts are really bad ideas for that.<br /> <br /> Spiritual Wrath - for example - requires a claw attack... so you need to shift in a lot of situations to even use it. Luna's Armor might grant you soak dice greater than shifting to Crinos or Hispo can... or might not... and you could use Steel Fur instead (pretty much the only reason to buy Steel Fur is that you can use it with Rage).<br /> <br /> The problem is these are generally less &quot;powerful opening moves&quot; and more either highly situational, or something a character is carefully built around to make use of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T17:21:26-07:00","id":1312450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1311149-do-you-allow-your-players-to-transform-instantly-into-crinos?p=1312443#post1312443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is most of the Gnosis based combat Gifts are really bad ideas for that.<br /> <br /> Spiritual Wrath - for example - requires a claw attack... so you need to shift in a lot of situations to even use it. Luna's Armor might grant you soak dice greater than shifting to Crinos or Hispo can... or might not... and you could use Steel Fur instead (pretty much the only reason to buy Steel Fur is that you can use it with Rage).<br /> <br /> The problem is these are generally less &quot;powerful opening moves&quot; and more either highly situational, or something a character is carefully built around to make use of.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Does anyone get Steel fur and Luna's armor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T17:35:46-07:00","id":1312456,"title":"","content":"Steel fur is Glass walkers<br /> Lunas armor - Child of Gaia, Silver Fang and Shadow Lord.<br /> <br /> But, less likely to buy steel for out of tribe, it gives a social penalty toward non Glass walkers, and it gives a Dex penalty<br /> It has the advantage of not needing Gnosis, but also .. Does Luna's armor still have the requirement of having the moon visible to activate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":16927,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","user":"Illithid","date":". 05-16-2019, 12:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T00:29:22-07:00","id":1312497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1311149-do-you-allow-your-players-to-transform-instantly-into-crinos?p=1312420#post1312420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That really only applies to monstrously fast enemies. After all, even without Gnosis expenditure, SotF adds a flat +10 to your initiative that will likely put you at the top of the list whatever you roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to be operating under the assumption that every character will have a level 2 Ahroun Gift, whereas a better assumption would be more Garou need to choose between Rage and Gnosis in a turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T01:45:35-07:00","id":1312510,"title":"","content":"Splitting your action to Shift is also handy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T01:59:53-07:00","id":1312511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1311149-do-you-allow-your-players-to-transform-instantly-into-crinos?p=1312497#post1312497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You seem to be operating under the assumption that every character will have a level 2 Ahroun Gift, whereas a better assumption would be more Garou need to choose between Rage and Gnosis in a turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, because that was the assumption you were replying to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-15T14:42:05-07:00","id":1331117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1311149-do-you-allow-your-players-to-transform-instantly-into-crinos?p=1312510#post1312510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Splitting your action to Shift is also handy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Splitting your action is super useful in all kinds of ways!<br /> <br /> But to get clarity on the rules as written: if you're going from homid to lupus, as a homid, not splitting actions or spending rage, would you have to succeed on four separate rolls, or just get a combined four successes on as many rolls as it takes, and that's how many turns it takes you? In the former case, it would always take at least four turns to get to lupus, but in the latter, you could get all the way to lupus in a single turn if you rolled four successes with your first try.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-15T14:45:49-07:00","id":1331118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1311149-do-you-allow-your-players-to-transform-instantly-into-crinos?p=1311182#post1311182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OF course Hispo is also a pretty awesome killing form too.</div> </div> </div> </div>It really is. I could totally see plenty of lupus preferring to fight in hispo over crinos if conditions don't warrant having opposable thumbs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-15T15:49:50-07:00","id":1331130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wilson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1311149-do-you-allow-your-players-to-transform-instantly-into-crinos?p=1331117#post1331117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But to get clarity on the rules as written: if you're going from homid to lupus, as a homid, not splitting actions or spending rage, would you have to succeed on four separate rolls, or just get a combined four successes on as many rolls as it takes, and that's how many turns it takes you? In the former case, it would always take at least four turns to get to lupus, but in the latter, you could get all the way to lupus in a single turn if you rolled four successes with your first try.</div> </div> </div> </div>Second option. You need four successes over however many rolls it takes you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T11:32:29-07:00","id":1487217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1311149-do-you-allow-your-players-to-transform-instantly-into-crinos?p=1312020#post1312020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, if we cherry pick the perfect selection of Gnosis based combat Gifts, it might be worth it to spend Gnosis on SotF and go first to use those instead of spending Rage on shifting. At least until you throw Chaos Mechanics into the mix and can do both.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile in normal play, SotF puts a combat focused Garou so high up the initiative roster every round with it's passive bonus, that they're going to act before 99.9% of things in the WoD that don't also have SotF, so they're not going to worry about the Gnosis option the vast majority of the time.<br /> <br /> Gnosis also isn't as free flowing as Rage or WP, so tossing 5 Gnosis out on the first round of combat is... probably not a great idea.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A bit of necromancy, but I didnt want to open a new tread for this matter.<br /> <br /> Spirit of the Fray offers a passive bonus to Initiative, so far so good.<br /> <br /> It also offers the possibility to spend Gnosis on an initiative roll, my questions are:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Is this new expenditure reflexive? It does not make sense to spend Gnosis to go first on the <i>next</i> turn initiative, I need to go first NOW.</li> <li>Do you need to keep spending Gnosis each turn for the extra +10, or does the first turn expenditure suffices?</li> </ol>I specially look forward to read <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar16927_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"16927\" data-vbnamecard=\"16927\">Illithid</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3118_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3118\" data-vbnamecard=\"3118\">Cifer</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar156_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"156\" data-vbnamecard=\"156\">Bunyip</a> opinions.<br /> <br /> Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 07-20-2022, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T12:31:23-07:00","id":1487229,"title":"","content":"The last post before you was three years ago, you can't count on the membership being the same.<br /> <br /> There's nothing in Spirit of the Fray that would suggest that it requires an action to spend Gnosis to pump up Initiative further; the point spent is for the turn where Initiative is being compared. By RAW, though, it only lasts for that one turn unless the ST rules otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T12:55:16-07:00","id":1487237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1311149-do-you-allow-your-players-to-transform-instantly-into-crinos?p=1487217#post1487217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this new expenditure reflexive?</div> </div> </div> </div>By my reading? Yes. It's not as explicit as it could be, but between the editions it tends to be phrased as being applicable that turn, which means if it isn't reflexive it's useless.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you need to keep spending Gnosis each turn for the extra +10, or does the first turn expenditure suffices? </div> </div> </div>Spending Gnosis applies to one round, not all of combat.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T17:53:46-07:00","id":1487289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1311149-do-you-allow-your-players-to-transform-instantly-into-crinos?p=1487237#post1487237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By my reading? Yes. It's not as explicit as it could be, but between the editions it tends to be phrased as being applicable that turn, which means if it isn't reflexive it's useless.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Spending Gnosis applies to one round, not all of combat.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks, this is what I was thinking, it ought to be reflexive or it is pointless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T00:58:41-07:00","id":1487324,"title":"","content":"From W20 page 268:<br /> <i>Technically, you can roll a new initiative each turn.<br /> To speed things along, though, you might decide to simply have everyone roll one initiative for that particular combat session and then stick with it for the rest of the scene. The Storyteller must decide which option applies before the action starts. Don\u2019t try to use both options within the same scene \u2014 it\u2019ll get messy.</i><br /> <br /> So, I read that as not rolling initiative each turn is the preferred version of combat. Spirit of the Frey is permanent. Meaning the option to add additional 10 to the initiative is permanently available to the character. It is not an action (although it prohibits Rage expanding in the given turn). So, it makes sense to spend the Gnosis when Initiative is determined (at the beginning of combat or each turn, if that option is chosen).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}